{
  "title": "Io {ip:sono} Marco e {ip:ho} vent'anni",
  "translation": "I am Marco and I am twenty years old",
  "topics": "Personal pronouns, essere and avere, numbers, age and quantities",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      "The personal pronouns are often left out, because the verb ending already shows the person: *{ip:Sono} italiano* is more natural than *Io {ip:sono} italiano*. Use them for emphasis or contrast. *Lei* with a capital letter is the polite *you*.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Pronoun",
            "Meaning",
            "essere (to be)",
            "avere (to have)"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "io",
              "I",
              "{ip:sono}",
              "{ip:ho}"
            ],
            [
              "tu",
              "you",
              "{ip:sei}",
              "{ip:hai}"
            ],
            [
              "lui / lei / Lei",
              "he / she / you (polite)",
              "{ip:è}",
              "{ip:ha}"
            ],
            [
              "noi",
              "we",
              "{ip:siamo}",
              "{ip:abbiamo}"
            ],
            [
              "voi",
              "you (plural)",
              "{ip:siete}",
              "{ip:avete}"
            ],
            [
              "loro",
              "they",
              "{ip:sono}",
              "{ip:hanno}"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "Careful: *{ip:è}* with an accent means *is*, while *e* means *and*. The *h* in *{ip:ho}, {ip:hai}, {ip:ha}, {ip:hanno}* is silent.",
      "In Italian, you have your age: *{ip:Ho} vent'anni* (I am twenty). Ask: *Quanti anni {ip:hai}?*",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "1–10",
            "11–20",
            "Tens"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "uno, due, tre, quattro, cinque",
              "undici, dodici, tredici, quattordici, quindici",
              "venti, trenta, quaranta"
            ],
            [
              "{ip:sei}, sette, otto, nove, dieci",
              "sedici, diciassette, diciotto, diciannove, venti",
              "cinquanta, sessanta, settanta, ottanta, novanta, cento"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "Quantities: *un po' di* pane (a little bread), *molto* pane / *molta* acqua (a lot of), *poco* tempo (little), *tanti* amici (many). Before a noun, *molto, poco* and *tanto* agree with it."
    ]
  },
